    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec adds a `bulkSignupWarning` flag to the owner-create response: `true` when more than 80 owners were already created that day, otherwise `false`. Since the acceptance test reads the value back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, it had to be **persisted** on the owner (following the exact pattern of the existing derived fields like `namesakeCount` and `customerCode`).\n\nChanges, all in `src/main`:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` boolean, `readOnly` property to the `Owner` schema (not `OwnerFields`, so it isn't a request input). The OpenAPI generator produces the matching `OwnerDto` getter/setter, and MapStruct auto-maps it by name.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `Boolean bulkSignupWarning` column (`bulk_signup_warning`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column. Tests run under the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change is what makes the column exist.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 captured the day's existing-owner count (the same `ownersRegisteredOn(registrationDate)` value already used for the daily-limit rule) and set `owner.setBulkSignupWarning(ownersRegisteredToday > 80)` before saving, gated by a named `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` constant.\n\nThe count is taken *before* the current owner is saved, so \"more than 80 already created today\" maps to a strict `> 80`. `mvnw test` is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 test passing, including the new `coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold` case).",
